<title>LATVIA: ESTONIA-LEKS CONSIDERS LITHUANIA DEAL.</title>
<headline>ESTONIA-LEKS CONSIDERS LITHUANIA DEAL.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estonian insurance company Leks said on Wednesday that it was considering buying a stake in an insurance company in Lithuania, similar to deal it just signed to buy 55 percent of Latvia's Saules Laiks.</p>
<p>&quot;We are looking at a similar arrangement in Lithuania and we are currently in talks which may be finalised during this year, in the autmumn,&quot; Leks chairman Raul Kastan told a news conference as he signed the deal to buy into Saules.</p>
<p>He declined to name the company with which Leks was negotiating.</p>
<p>-- Riga newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
